Smallest R_LRS that fits the default 12F cell: 6,000 ohm.
Below that the select transistor, not the resistor, sets cell area.

HOW TO READ THIS
  Moving right buys area and loses signal. The calibration makes
  the loading column irrelevant to ACCURACY -- calibrated accuracy
  should stay flat across the sweep -- so R_LRS can be chosen on
  area and ADC-resolvability alone. That freedom is the
  contribution; without the correction the raw column forces a
  high resistance for accuracy reasons.

